
# Intelligent Courier Planning System

## 1. Problem Statement
The system optimizes courier parcel selection and delivery routes using
Design and Analysis of Algorithms.

## 2. Objectives
- Prioritize parcels using Merge Sort.
- Select optimal parcels using 0/1 Knapsack.
- Calculate shortest paths using Dijkstra.
- Optimize delivery order using Nearest Neighbor TSP.
- Compare algorithm execution times.

## 3. Input
- Parcel ID
- Parcel weight
- Priority
- Delivery deadline
- Parcel value
- Delivery location

## 4. Algorithms
| Algorithm | Purpose | Complexity |
|---|---|---|
| Merge Sort | Parcel sorting | O(n log n) |
| 0/1 Knapsack DP | Parcel selection | O(nW) |
| Dijkstra (heap) | Shortest paths | O((V+E) log V) |
| Nearest Neighbor | Route approximation | O(k^2) |

## 5. Graph Design
The delivery network is represented using a weighted,
undirected adjacency list.

## 6. Expected Output
- Sorted parcels
- Selected parcels
- Total package weight
- Shortest delivery paths
- Optimized delivery sequence
- Total route distance
- Runtime comparison

## 7. Conclusion
The proposed system combines multiple algorithms to
simulate an intelligent courier planning application.
